:1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"HOX068\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"The answer says the board selects the auditor 'by a majority vote of trustees who are not \\\"interested persons\\\"'. That is selection by the independent trustees under §32(a), so the point is covered.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0,\"reason\":\"The answer never says that an all-independent audit committee permits omitting ratification under Rule 32a-4. It ties omission only to there being no annual meeting.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":0,\"reason\":\"Optional point not addressed: nothing on the trust-wide vote or on series using different auditors. This does not reduce the grade.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Point 1 is fully covered by the independent-trustee majority vote, so required coverage is 1 of 2, which meets the half threshold. Point 2's Rule 32a-4 audit-committee basis for omitting ratification is missing. The no-annual-meeting route matches §32(a)'s text and is not a falsehood. Nothing says shareholders must always ratify, and selection is not assigned to the adviser, so there is no central error.\"}","ttft_ms":3701,"type":"result","duration_ms":6956,"uuid":"e9fdbb55-3acd-49c6-a4d3-8d68469cae2d","ttft_stream_ms":541,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":541,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
